id: pm-jira-2m0s
title: The deprecated jira-sync importer alias loses its credential gate when the preflight override is scoped
description: "Found by auditing the class after CodeRabbit reported the same defect in pm-linear. Scoping registerPreflight to a command list narrows which commands the override runs for. The scope listed jira sync, jira import and jira export, but registerImporter also exposes the deprecated config-driven jira-sync alias, which reaches the same network pull. The previously global registration covered it by accident. isMutatingJiraInvocation also returned false for the alias, so even a global registration would not have failed fast on it. Both are now fixed: the alias is in the scope list and the classifier treats it as mutating on the same dry-run terms as jira import. A loop test binds the scope list to the classifier so the two cannot drift apart."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-14T06:44:38.580Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-14T06:44:40.220Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-14T06:44:40.206Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-14T06:44:40.206Z"
author: claude
resolution: jira-sync import added to the preflight scope and recognised as mutating by isMutatingJiraInvocation.
expected_result: "A mutating legacy jira-sync import fails fast without credentials, exactly as jira import does."
actual_result: Scope and classifier both cover the alias; a loop test asserts every scoped command is classified mutating so the lists cannot drift.
